> "The baguette build at $7,930 is the ring I would buy myself. The escalating baguettes extend the emerald cut's horizontal geometry all the way to the edges of the finger. It reads as one continuous Art Deco statement, not a center stone with side stones. If you want a vintage emerald cut ring that looks like it came from a 1930s estate sale — this is it. New stone, new metal, old soul." — Farzana Hasan, **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**

