## Expert Summary

The vintage emerald cut diamond ring is the most coherent category in the emerald cut family. Every element points in the same direction. The stone is Art Deco by design.

The settings are Art Deco by craft. The combination does not require compromise or inspiration. It requires alignment.

The GIA-certified natural path starts at $4,330 complete — the [1ct D-VS1 at $3,140](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29333987?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) paired with the [Art Deco Fleur-De-Lis at $1,190](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/art-deco-inspired-fleur-de-lis-pave-vintage-style-engagement-ring-in-14k-rose-gold-by-james-allen-item-315297?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). The best overall natural build is $5,455 — the same stone with the [Hand-Engraved Micropavé Platinum](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/hand-engraved-micropave-diamond-engagement-ring-in-platinum-1-6-ct-tw-item-194236?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). That setting has 108 confirmed reviews and passes the Milgrain Test.

It is the most authentically Art Deco build available in a new certified ring.

The lab path delivers more stone for less money at every price point. The [1.94ct F-VVS1 lab emerald at $2,229](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29147824?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) in the Art Deco Fleur-De-Lis setting totals $3,419 complete. That is a near-2ct stone, F-VVS1 clarity, in a 102-review Art Deco setting for less than a natural 1ct stone alone.

The vintage look is entirely in the setting. The lab stone delivers it identically.

The Baguette Bridge is the highest expression of this ring. Escalating baguette side stones extend the emerald cut's geometry along the finger in a way that no other side stone achieves. At [$7,930 complete in white gold](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/escalating-baguette-side-stone-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-310913?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) or [$9,750 in platinum with a lab 2ct D-FL](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28828463?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), this is the ring that looks like an estate piece.

It is new in every material. It is Art Deco in every line.

